    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d755">

                <pb facs="0839" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg751"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.81 Buenos Aires/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Buenos Aires</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-18T13:00:00-04:00">October 18, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 18—12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. From Commercial Attaché for Commerce. Finance Minister has prohibited
                    issuance of exchange permits for remittance of any funds whatever which were
                    blocked prior to May 1, 1933, because such would be contrary to Roca agreement.
                    Not believed, however, that this refers to documentary bills.</p>
                <p>Although opposed by the more conservative elements, a meeting of the American
                    importers here called for tomorrow as the result of which it is expected a
                    delegation will call on Ambassador insisting that some action be taken by the
                    Embassy to secure more exchange for American interests.<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d755-f1"/> Dye.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d755-f1" n="28" xml:id="d755-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 15 from the Commercial Attaché”, transmitted in telegram of
                    November 2, 6 p.m., from the Consul at Buenos Aires, <ref target="#pg762">p.
                        762</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
